{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/841943-changing-breeds-and-appearance","id":841943,"title":"Changing Breeds and Appearance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T09:33:48-08:00","id":841943,"title":"Changing Breeds and Appearance","content":"So, this is more of a cosmetic/roleplaying question. The Garou characters demonstrate a pretty wide range of body types (obviously with most being fit) but height and weight does vary considerably with certain Tribes having some more common traits. But since some of the Changing Breeds seem to be somewhat more specific, I was wondering how people handle their appearances. Should all Nagah be and sinewy for instance?<br /> <br /> Inspiration for this question came with some of the people I play with talking about what a Gurahl character should look like. Forest Walkers tend to be shorter and stockier but the general description for the Breed says that Gurahl tend to be at the high end of height ranges and thick boned. There was some debate among the group as to what constituted &quot;tall&quot; and &quot;big.&quot; Some thought 6'2 was a suitable tall height while others insisted on closer to 6'5 and above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:16:20-08:00","id":842183,"title":"","content":"I think it's because the changing breeds are more tied to their &quot;breed&quot; rather then werewolf who are tied to their &quot;culture&quot;. There is also the whole animism aspect too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T11:00:05-08:00","id":843523,"title":"","content":"It probably goes toward the simple biological aspect of 'like attracts like' (for the most part) and sociological 'my parents and friends all say this is desirable'. Gurahl see the pro-wrestler build as desirable because biology says 'this makes a good partner for breeding' and because their society has promoted it. Nagah would be the same with a gymnasts build. <br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind, that 'average' is what is given. But notable characters in a story aren't notable because they are 'average', and sometimes weird things happen. The fact is, their human form is still human. They'll still run the same ranges as human, just with a skewed 'average'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:42:24-08:00","id":845453,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the human body shape will reflect the animal form, or vice versa, at least in regards to animal attributes somehow manifesting similarly.<br /> <br /> There are thin Garou, stocky Garou, and the likes. Most Garou tend to eventually raise up their physical attributes (because they are very physical warriors, typically), so they wind up looking very muscular and stocky as they gain experience.<br /> <br /> Other Fera may be more lithe, but that may be more about the training and lifestyles than their animal features. A Nuwisha could be a fat man, but the typical &quot;trickster&quot; likely needs to be a bit more fit than that. A Khan could be skinny too, but as a noble warrior king who's intent on presenting himself as an impressive warrior, he's more apt to look like Dwayne Johnson than Andrew Garfield. A Gurahl could very well be a big, stocky man/woman because that's the lifestyle that best suits the needs too.<br /> <br /> That's just my take on it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"J